TEXT -2408 -248 Left 2 ;shunt resistor
TEXT -2552 -784 Left 1 ;The 0.5Omhs shunt resistor senses the load current, while the \nRa-Rb voltage divider scales the AC supply voltage to produce\nthe current and voltage sensing signals, Vis, Vvs.\n0.5ohms can be made with two 1 ohm resistors in series.\nDesired ratio was 20.78 for voltage sensing branch, 56K & 2.7k give us\na ratio of 20.74.
TEXT -2536 280 Left 1 ;Two LM324 differential amplifiers level-shift the sensed current \nand voltage signals by 2.1 V and scale them to suitable voltage ranges\nfor ADC measurement.\nValues for R1-R2 were chosen to give us a Peak to peak voltage of 2V\nValues for R5-R7 to allow us to introduce a 2.1V offset.
TEXT -1336 -800 Left 1 ;Two first-order low-pass RC filters with a cut-off frequency\nof approximately 10 kHz attenuate high-frequency noise while\npreserving the 500 Hz measured signals.\nchoose resistor value of 16K ohms, and 1nF for the capicator to get \ndesired corner frequency.
TEXT -1320 -40 Left 1 ;A half-wave rectifier, smoothing capacitor and LT1085-5 linear \nregulator convert the AC supply into a regulated 5 V DC supply \nfor the analogue circuitry.
TEXT -304 -784 Left 1 ;An voltage divider generates approximately 2.1 V from the \nregulated 5 V supply, while the LM324 voltage follower provides a stable,\nlow-impedance offset reference.
TEXT -96 -208 Left 2 ;Voltage Follower
TEXT -296 688 Left 1 ;The LM324 operates as an open-loop comparator, producing a square-wave \noutput whose rising and falling edges correspond to the zero crossings of \nthe AC supply voltage.
TEXT -32 144 Left 2 ;Testing
